From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: leave a lost compositor to the client

check_fatal_error() aborted on any display error, including the compositor
going away or restarting. That is not a bug in the client, and the toolkit
sees the same error on the connection. browser_shell left a core dump for
every compositor restart, from readQueue() under eglSwapBuffers().

Abort on a protocol error only, which is a real client bug. Otherwise hand the
failure to the caller. dequeueBuffer() has to take it now: it looped on
readQueue(true) until a buffer came free, which would never end with the
connection gone.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/egl/platforms/wayland/wayland_window.cpp
+++ b/egl/platforms/wayland/wayland_window.cpp
@@ -80,7 +80,12 @@ int WaylandNativeWindow::dequeueBuffer(BaseNativeWindowBuffer **buffer, int *fen
 
     while (m_freeBufs==0) {
         HYBRIS_TRACE_COUNTER("wayland-platform", "m_freeBufs", "%i", m_freeBufs);
-        readQueue(true);
+        if (readQueue(true) < 0) {
+            HYBRIS_TRACE_END("wayland-platform", "dequeueBuffer_wait_for_buffer", "");
+            HYBRIS_TRACE_END("wayland-platform", "dequeueBuffer", "");
+            unlock();
+            return -1;
+        }
     }
 
     std::list<WaylandNativeWindowBuffer *>::iterator it = m_bufList.begin();
--- a/platforms/wayland/wayland_window_common.cpp
+++ b/platforms/wayland/wayland_window_common.cpp
@@ -149,6 +149,13 @@ static void check_fatal_error(struct wl_display *display)
     if (error == 0)
         return;
 
+    /* The compositor went away, or restarted. That is no bug in this client and
+     * not this library's call: the toolkit sees the same error on the connection
+     * and can shut down in order, keeping its data. Say so to the caller instead,
+     * which has nothing left to draw to. */
+    if (error != EPROTO)
+        return;
+
     fprintf(stderr, "Wayland display got fatal error %i: %s\n", error, strerror(error));
 
     if (errno != 0)
--- a/vulkan/platforms/wayland/wayland_window.cpp
+++ b/vulkan/platforms/wayland/wayland_window.cpp
@@ -86,7 +86,12 @@ int WaylandNativeWindow::dequeueBuffer(BaseNativeWindowBuffer **buffer, int *fen
 
     while (m_freeBufs==0) {
         HYBRIS_TRACE_COUNTER("wayland-platform", "m_freeBufs", "%i", m_freeBufs);
-        readQueue(true);
+        if (readQueue(true) < 0) {
+            HYBRIS_TRACE_END("wayland-platform", "dequeueBuffer_wait_for_buffer", "");
+            HYBRIS_TRACE_END("wayland-platform", "dequeueBuffer", "");
+            unlock();
+            return -1;
+        }
     }
 
     std::list<WaylandNativeWindowBuffer *>::iterator it = m_bufList.begin();
